      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Heart rate monitoring in wellness chairs often uses heat-sensing or photoplethysmography (PPG) technology, which can be affected by the angle and proximity to your body. To minimize the signal, try sitting with your arms close to your sides, covering the armrests, or wearing a well-fitting warm clothing to slightly raise your body temperature, which may throw off the readings. Alternatively, you can try techniques like deep breathing, meditation, or simply relaxing your arm muscles to reduce any natural variations.",
